From 489186178777821594d5705ef8e9d17ced6ac3d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GiggleHacks <GiggleHacks@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 06:33:54 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] mod_freebeforeload: free the previous map before loading the
 next one

A map change kept the old world model, its lightmaps and its textures until
the new map had finished loading (Mod_PurgeUnused at the end of signon,
R_SkinFrame_Purge in R_Modules_NewMap), so it needed the memory of both maps
at once: about 900 MB more than either map on the maps this was measured on.

mod_freebeforeload (default 0, behaviour unchanged):
 1  SV_SpawnServer unloads the previous world model and purges the textures
    only it used before it loads the next world. A client of a remote server
    unloads every model the new map does not use as soon as it has the new
    precache list, before loading anything.
 2  when hosting, every model is unloaded first (lowest peak; models both
    maps use are loaded again).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
